2026-11-27T10:17:32.5302322Z -- Today's cheaper windows and the lighting window
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5302672Z   ok   a day with two cheaper runs gives two windows, each contiguous run once
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5303017Z   ok   the lighting window opens the default 60 min before the first window and closes at its start
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5303483Z   ok   the lead time is the configured option
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5303953Z   ok   a lead inside [0, a day] is its own: 0 lights at the window's start, 240 four hours before, and a day's lead lights now
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5305109Z   ok   a stored lead outside [0, a day] is the default 60 min: 1e12 does not overflow the window's datetime, and a negative or NaN lead is not one
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5305792Z   ok   a window open at the plan's first step lights now, never in the past
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5306216Z   ok   a cheaper step while the pump is planned off is not a window
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5306495Z   ok   a cheaper step tomorrow is counted but is not one of today's windows
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5306866Z   ok   today is the local day: at UTC+1 the 23:00 UTC step is tomorrow, and the window is published in local time
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5307295Z   ok   a naive plan stamp is UTC under a non-UTC host zone: the windows and the lighting window equal the aware build's
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5307713Z   ok   a one-step plan has no measurable step, so it gives no window (and does not index a second stamp)
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5308084Z   ok   null control: a day wood never beats the pump gives no windows and no lighting window
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5308420Z   ok   the wood sensor publishes the windows and the lighting window as attributes
2026-11-27T10:17:32.5308730Z   ok   and with no window it publishes an empty list and no lighting window
